re of the  relationship between humans and Titans  is brought into question of course we  later learned that every single Titan  even the mindless Titans who roam around  aimlessly like big dumb sacs of flesh  were once human beings every Titan was  once a human who was turned into a Titan  against their will and as titans these  humans have virtually no control over  their actions they suddenly become  mindless beasts who devour human flesh  even though this is something they never  would have done as humans this  complicates the whole villain situation  even further yes the Titans as they are  right now are a menace and an  existential threat to humans unless the  humans kill these Titans they will most  likely be killed themselves and killing  the Titans in self-defense is something  the humans behind the walls are forced  to do at the same time killing a Titan  is the same as killing the innocent  human who had been turned into that  specific Titan against their own will so  even if you kill them out of  self-defense because you have to you  can't exactly be happy about it and  what's more we can't exactly consider  these regular Titans to be the ultimate  evil in attack on Titan because as  humans they were not evil they did not  choose to be turned into Titans and once  they were turned into Titans they became  mindless monsters simply following their  natural urge to consume humans a  mindless Titan attacking a human is no  more evil than a hungry wolf attacking a  chicken coop at the same time that we  are learning more about the Titans and  how they came to exist in the first  place we also learned that there are  some extremely evil humans behind the  walls  although these humans are not mindless  beasts and although they enjoy all the  benefits of human intelligence reason  and emotion these humans choose to do  terrible things to other humans look no  further than the corrupt government  behind the walls and the first interior  squad who have no problem 