e not necessarily doing what they  chose to do but rather they appear to be  doing something that has been thrust  upon them by someone else as the story  progresses we meet the beast Titan  another Titan shifter and eventually we  learned the truth about Annie bertolt  Reiner and where they really come from  the three of them come from beyond the  walls and they grew up in a country that  discriminated against them and treated  them like inferior and dangerous people  for no other reason than the fact that  they were born as ldiots they spent  their childhood being indoctrinated by  male propaganda which tried to convince  them that all LD ins are inherently evil  and that the only way for them to atone  for the sins of their kind is to help  Marly destroy the LD ins on the island  they entered the merlion warrior program  which was designed in order to recruit  LD ins who would be willing to fight for  Marlay as Titan shifters because only LD  ants could become Titans Marly had to  rely on LD ins to compete with each  other in order to determine who should  Herot one of the titan shifter powers  the reward for LD ins who passed the  warrior program and succeeded in  inheriting one of the titan shifter  powers was honorary male and citizenship  for themselves and their families which  meant that their families could finally  stop living in horrible conditions and  could actually afford food medicine and  other basic necessities when Annie  Bertolt and Reiner came to the island of  paradise they truly believed that they  were not going to be hurting people but  rather evil Devils who are a threat to  the entire world well it's likely that  Annie didn't feel this way and that she  saw through Marlin propaganda but Reiner  definitely felt for these lies at first  it is only after the three shifters  infiltrated the walls and came to  realize that the people behind the walls  were just normal people like everyone  else that Reiner Annie and Berthold  could be said to have had a choice at  this point  they could have abandoned their mission  because they realized that they were  being asked to kill innocent people or  they could have continued abandoning the  mission would have likely caused  problems for their families back in  Marlay but I believe that abandoning the  mission after realizing what the people  behind the walls were really like would  have been the right thing to do  continuing to follow Marla's orders  after realizing that the LD ins were not  Devils just normal people like everyone  else was a choice and I believe that it  was the wrong choice  Annie Reiner and Bertolt can be  legitimately criticized for continuing  on with the mission even after spending  years in the 104th training corps and  befriending so many LD ends on the  island but the fact that the three of  them did have regrets and in some cases  these regrets led to the development of  serious and lasting mental problems  proves that Reiner Annie and Bertolt are  not just evil monsters they are not  ruthless villains in spite of their  immoral actions they are human beings  who found themselves in a difficult and  tragic situation and who made some bad  choices in my opinion and that brings us  to the real evil behind the entire  mission to infiltrate the walls the  marlins  in many ways the marlins and especially  their government and military are the  closest thing that we have to an  outright villain in attack on titan the  way that the Marlins treat the LD ins is  inexcusable  the way that they expect innocent LD ins  to continuously pay for the supposed  sins of their ancient ancestors is  ludicrous we are not sure how much of  the history that Marly claims is true is  fact and how much is fiction but  regardless of what happened in the past  the way that Marlins treat the  audience's inhumane and unjustifiable  there are summer lands like general Theo  McGrath who are more tolerant towards  ldiots but on the whole we have seen  everyone from members of the military  and security forces to ordinary janitors  on the streets abusing LD ins including  LD and children not only that but  despite hating the audience the Marlins  are still not above using LD ins and  their ability to transform into Titans  as a weapon against rival nations in  fact Marla has used both the Titan  shifter powers and the power of the  mindless Titans to become a great  military power and to subjugate other  nations to its rule so to put it simply  kamar lay seriously  but as much as I hate the government  military and security forces of Marlay  for being opportunistic militaristic  supremacists we have to acknowledge that  even Marlay has  innocent civilians including children so  even if war against them is just we have  to remember that every war will result  in civilian casualties also I would love  to say that Marlins are so obviously the  bad guys that it's unrealistic for them  to ever exist in the real world but  sadly all we need to do is look back to  World War Two and we will see that a  regime as insane and evil as Marlay is  not just fiction aside from the  government of Marlay being clear  villains in my opinion recent chapters  of the manga have forced us to  repeatedly reevaluate the role of aaron  and his half-brother Zeke in the attack  on Titan story Aaron started out as the  protagonist and Zeke started out as a  villain however in recent chapters Aaron  and Zeke have teamed up and their goal  is supposedly to carry out Zeke's master  plan although I'm not sure that Aaron  will ultimately go along with Zeke's  insane plan but let's talk about Aaron  first after realizing the truth about  the outside world Aaron had a choice he  could stay on paradies and wait from our  lands to keep attacking the island until  eventually Marley's modern technology  and remaining titan powers destroyed  every L  on the island or he could do something  to strike back against the enemy and  defend the island Aaron decided on the  latter he infiltrated Marlay by  pretending to be a wounded veteran and  he established contact with his  half-brother Zeke who was also plotting  against Marley together they launched an  attack on the burial captured the  Warhammer Titan power and with the help  of armen's colossal titan they destroyed  a large chunk of Marley's army however  in the process of capturing the  Warhammer Titan a lot of innocent people  including LD ins were killed in Lipari  oh these casualties were a direct result  of Aaron's decision not to sit back and  to take the war to the enemy so this is  a burden that he now must bear on his  shoulders on top of that after consuming  the Warhammer Titan Aaron's personality  changed with three Titan powers inside  of him Aaron's mine is filled with the  memories of hundreds of previous Titan  shifters and he has recently begun to  appear mentally unstable and if that  wasn't enough as he has gotten closer to  Zeke Aaron has deliberately distanced  himself from his closest friends  including Mikasa and Armin Aaron  insulted Mikasa by insinuating that she  only defends him because her Ackerman  jeans are biologically programmed to do  it and when Armin protested against  Aaron's behavior Aaron physically  assaulted Armin all of this has raised  questions about whether Aaron has come  full circle and become the embodiment of  the famous saying from The Dark Knight  you either die a hero or live long  enough to see yourself become the  villain and once we learned what Zeke's  ultimate plan actually is if Aaron  really supports it then it isn't hard to  make the argument that Aaron has become  the villain now let's look at Zeke as we  know Zeke had a very tough childhood  because his father intended to use him  as nothing more than a tool to help the  LDN restoration is to destroy Marlay and  at a very young age Zeke was forced to  betray his own parents to the  authorities in order to save his own  life and the lives of his grandparents  after that 