ainst all his life and  in his mind he has come to accept that  there is something wrong with the  audience in reality there is something  wrong with those individuals who choose  to abuse and discriminate against  innocent people the fault does not live  with the people who are being abused  so is Zeke a villain yes if this is  really his plan then I would call him a  villain albeit a villain who is a  traumatized and tortured soul we can all  understand how Zeke's traumatic life has  led him to do the things he has done  but just because we can understand that  his life was difficult doesn't mean that  we should support the genocide or plan  that he wants to implement  on his own people Zeke might have turned  against Marley but his plan is in line  with the wishes of the most viciously  aunty L D and Marlins it is ironic that  throughout his childhood Zeke suffered  discrimination at the hands of the  Marlins including being forced to wear a  special armband when in public so that  everyone would know that he was LD and  these armbands are part of the reason  why Zeke faced abuse and discrimination  on a daily basis from aggressive Marlins  for instance in Chapter 114 we see an  instance when a young Zeke and his  parents were out on a rooftop of a  building overlooking the barrio just  talking and enjoying the view and then  mr lay and janitor sees their arm bends  he instantly attacks them throwing water  all over them and insulting them he  demands to know how these descendents of  the devil would dare to reproduce and  have more children  the janitor believed that the LD ins  were inherently evil this part of the  devil and that they shouldn't be allowed  to even have children this was a deeply  traumatizing experience for Zeke and yet  as an adult he is essentially carrying  out the wishes of that Marley and  janitor to make the irony complete after  Zeke tainted some wine with his spinal  fluid so that key members of the survey  corps on paradise would turn into Titans  as soon as he screamed those LD ins who  consumed the wine were required to wear  black armbands to differentiate them  from those who didn't drink the wine how  sad and ironic that after living through  the cruel treatment that the audience  faced in Marley including being forced  to wear armbands to prove that they are  different from everyone else  Zeke decided to pursue a plan that the  very Marlins who abused him and his  family would have wholeheartedly  supported and because of Zeke other LD  ins were forced to wear armbands in  order to be differentiated from their  fellow human beings  so yes Zeke is a villain but he is a  villain who was created by the  traumatizing and abusive circumstances  of his life the fact that he is the  beast Titan and the fact that he has a  plan that I would consider villainous  suggests that Zeke is the real monster  in attack on Titan although he is a  monster of maar león and grisha's making  the thing that differentiates human from  wild beasts and from the mindless Titans  is their ability to choose the right  path in life but Zeke wants to take that  choice away  from his own people by forcing them  never to reproduce again and this is so  similar to the Marlins taking away so  many basic human choices and freedoms  from the ldiots the real question is  what will Eren do now personally I agree  with Armin  I think Aaron is pretending to go along  with Zeek because he needs his help  especially since Zeke has royal blood  which allows Aaron to harness the power  of the founding Titan but ultimately I  believe that Aaron will reject Zeke's  euthanasia plan and I believe that he  will do his best to find a solution that  will allow the LD ins to coexist with  the other nations ironically the real  monsters an attack on Titan are not the  giant man-eating Titans the real  monsters and villains are humans like  the Malayan military and government or  members of the first interior squad who  are willing to torture 